Q: How to pass a custom Parcelable object in Jetpack Compose Type-Safe Navigation (Navigation 2.8.0+)? A: <p>To pass a custom `Parcelable` in Compose Navigation 2.8.0+, you must define a custom `NavType` that tells the `NavHost` how to serialize your object to a string (usually via JSON) and how to deserialize it back out of the `Bundle`.</p>
<p>Here is a reusable, generic implementation for any `Parcelable` class using Kotlinx Serialization:</p>
<p>### 1. Create a Generic NavType Builder</p>
<p>Create this utility function in your project. It handles the `Bundle` extraction and the URI-encoding required for safe navigation.</p>
<pre><code>import android.os.Build
import android.os.Bundle
import android.os.Parcelable
import android.net.Uri
import androidx.navigation.NavType
import kotlinx.serialization.KSerializer
import kotlinx.serialization.json.Json

inline fun &lt;reified T : Parcelable&gt; customNavType(
    serializer: KSerializer&lt;T&gt;,
    isNullableAllowed: Boolean = false
): NavType&lt;T&gt; = object : NavType&lt;T&gt;(isNullableAllowed = isNullableAllowed) {

    override fun get(bundle: Bundle, key: String): T? =
        if (Build.VERSION.SDK_INT &gt;= Build.VERSION_CODES.TIRAMISU) {
            bundle.getParcelable(key, T::class.java)
        } else {
            @Suppress(&quot;DEPRECATION&quot;)
            bundle.getParcelable(key)
        }

    override fun parseValue(value: String): T {
        val decodedValue = Uri.decode(value)
        return Json.decodeFromString(serializer, decodedValue)
    }

    override fun put(bundle: Bundle, key: String, value: T) {
        bundle.putParcelable(key, value)
    }

    override fun serializeAsValue(value: T): String {
        val jsonString = Json.encodeToString(serializer, value)
        return Uri.encode(jsonString)
    }
}
</code></pre>
<p>### 2. Register the Type in your NavHost</p>
<p>When you define your `composable` destination, you must pass a `typeMap` that links your custom class to the new `NavType`.</p>
<pre class="lang-kotlin prettyprint-override"><code>val UserDataNavType = customNavType&lt;UserData&gt;(UserData.serializer())

NavHost(
    navController = navController,
    startDestination = Route.HomeScreen
) {
    composable&lt;Route.DetailsScreen&gt;(
        typeMap = mapOf(typeOf&lt;UserData&gt;() to UserDataNavType)
    ) { backStackEntry -&gt;
        // The library automatically parses the argument back into your object!
        val route = backStackEntry.toRoute&lt;Route.DetailsScreen&gt;()
        DetailsScreen(userData = route.userData)
    }
}
</code></pre>
<p>### 3. Navigate</p>
<p>Now you can simply pass the object directly into the navigate call:</p>
<pre class="lang-kotlin prettyprint-override"><code>val myUser = UserData(id = 1, name = &quot;John&quot;)
navController.navigate(Route.DetailsScreen(userData = myUser))
</code></pre>
<p>Make sure your `UserData` class is annotated with both `@Parcelize` and `@Serializable`.</p>
